body:
Once the SelectorExpr branches above are removed, `baseTypeName` only needs to resolve `*dst.Ident` — its SelectorExpr case exists solely to support the now-removed qualified-generic-receiver case (`*pkg.Gen[T]`), which is equally illegal Go and unreachable.

```suggestion
// baseTypeName returns the unqualified type name of expr when it is an
// Ident (MyStruct), used to resolve the base of a generic receiver's
// type-parameter list.
func baseTypeName(expr dst.Expr) (string, bool) {
	if ident, ok := expr.(*dst.Ident); ok {
		return ident.Name, true
	}
	return "", false
}
```

