Two things here: these three cases assert a positive match on illegal-Go qualified receivers, which should flip to `""` once the SelectorExpr matchers are removed. More importantly, this table has no coverage for `ParenExpr` receivers (`func (r (T)) M()`, `func (r (*T)) M()`) — the shape that actually compiles, actually appears in unformatted third-party source, and is the real crash this PR's `findFuncDecl` fix (return no-match instead of fataling) protects against. Verified both forms build with `go build` and parse to `*dst.ParenExpr` via this package's own parser, with `stripGenericTypes` already returning `""` for them.

