Now that matching happens before any mutation, this could go one step further:
`ParseDirectiveTemplate` doesn't depend on anything `addRuleImports` produces, so
validating the template before adding imports closes the remaining window where a
matched-but-invalid-template rule leaves an import spec in `root.Decls` before failing.
Currently harmless — `instrument()` aborts the whole file on any rule error, so the AST
mutation never reaches disk — but it keeps the "validate before mutate" invariant this fix
establishes fully intact, rather than partially.

```suggestion
